94
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:36,640
the number of gamma rays hitting the

95
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:38,959
scintillation crystal can actually be

96
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:40,720
more than the system can handle. This

97
00:03:38,959 --> 00:03:43,519
happens because the gamma camera needs

98
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:45,360
some time to recover between events. If

99
00:03:43,519 --> 00:03:46,959
two scintillation events happen too

100
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:48,799
close together, they can't both get

101
00:03:46,959 --> 00:03:51,360
recorded.

102
00:03:48,799 --> 00:03:53,599
The total dead time, which we call toao,

103
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:56,799
is given by this equation. Tao equals

104
00:03:53,599 --> 00:03:59,519
capital n minus small n / small n *

105
00:03:56,799 --> 00:04:02,560
capital n. So let me say it again. Tao

106
00:03:59,519 --> 00:04:04,959
equals capital n minus small n / small n

107
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:07,439
* capital n.

108
00:04:04,959 --> 00:04:09,280
Here capital n is the true count rate

109
00:04:07,439 --> 00:04:12,000
which means how many centilations

110
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:13,760
actually happen every second. Small n is

111
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,239
the observed count rate. So that's how

112
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:18,160
many the system actually records. If you

113
00:04:16,239 --> 00:04:20,160
take one divided by a small n, you get

114
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:21,840
the average time spent on each counted

115
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:24,160
event.

116
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:25,759
If you take one divided by capital n,

117
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:28,000
that's what you'd have in an ideal

118
00:04:25,759 --> 00:04:29,520
system without any dead time. The

119
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,360
difference between these two tells us

120
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:33,280
how much measurement is lost because of

121
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:35,360
