00:45:39,440 --> 00:45:43,440
Let's move into the fourth part where we

1215
00:45:41,359 --> 00:45:46,800
discuss system architecture and scatter

1216
00:45:43,440 --> 00:45:49,359
correction in spec and PET imaging.

1217
00:45:46,800 --> 00:45:51,440
This topic is pretty straightforward. We

1218
00:45:49,359 --> 00:45:53,359
focus on how these imaging systems are

1219
00:45:51,440 --> 00:45:55,520
built and the basic principles behind

1220
00:45:53,359 --> 00:45:57,520
scatter correction which is a major

1221
00:45:55,520 --> 00:46:00,839
technical consideration for accurate

1222
00:45:57,520 --> 00:46:00,839
image reconstruction.

1223
00:46:02,880 --> 00:46:07,599
On this slide you see a great picture of

1224
00:46:04,880 --> 00:46:10,000
a spec scanner. The spec camera system

1225
00:46:07,599 --> 00:46:12,000
is held together by a sturdy structure

1226
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:14,160
and it's designed to rotate around the

1227
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:16,079
